course: dictionary
lesson: 15980
title: Uppermost: the very top
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Uppermost means highest, or at the very top. The ending -most points to the very top of a group, like the top of a stack.
explain: «The uppermost shelf is the one nearest the ceiling.» Which shelf is the top one? The one closest to the ceiling, so uppermost means highest.
explain: Uppermost can also mean most important in someone's mind. «Safety was uppermost in her thoughts.» She thought about safety more than anything else. Check by swapping in a simple word: put most important or highest in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Uppermost means highest, or at the very top.
fact: «Uppermost» can also mean most important in someone's mind, as in «uppermost in my mind».
fact: «Uppermost» can be an adverb: «Lay the card face uppermost» means put it with the front facing up.
fact: In science, the uppermost layer of rock or soil is the top one, and it is usually the youngest.
fact: Useful phrases: «the uppermost layer», «right side uppermost», «uppermost in my mind».
exercise: «The uppermost shelf is the one nearest the ceiling.» What does uppermost mean here? | Wooden | Empty | Lowest, at the bottom | *Highest, at the very top
exercise: «Safety was uppermost in her thoughts.» What does uppermost mean here? | Highest up | Hidden | Fast | *Most important
exercise: Mum says, «Lay the card face uppermost.» What should you do? | Put it face down under the book | *Put it with the front side facing up | Hide it in a drawer | Throw it away
test: «The uppermost floor of the building has the best view.» Which floor is this? | Ground floor | Basement | *Top floor | Garden
test: «Her uppermost thought was getting home to her dog.» What did she think about most? | Her new shoes | *Getting home to her dog | The weather forecast | The school bus timetable
exam: In «Put the photo face uppermost on the table», what does uppermost mean? | Facing the wall | *Facing upwards, on top | Hidden under the table | Torn at the edges
